tags: $:/tags/Global
title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/modules/realm-scopes

<!-- Shared realm-scoping vocabulary. Two families: SCOPE LISTS — raw filters whose output is the allowed realm tags plus the `no-realm` sentinel when realm-less items are included; consumers split with !match[no-realm] / match[no-realm]. SCOPING ARITHMETIC — hgsd-scope-include/exclude reduce <scope-base> by <scope-tags>; both must be $let at the evaluation site (they are ambient variables, not parameters). Consumers: $hgsd.pick, $hgsd.pick-field, $hgsd.list, the realm-warning globe, and any extension via the realm-scope attribute (Boilerplate: realm scoping). Position rules: the selection's pristine marker runs FIRST (:then never short-circuits on accumulated output); the state read uses [title[X]…] mid-filter; :then[subfilter<…>] because a procedure's raw value is filter TEXT, not an evaluated list. -->
\procedure hgsd-realm-all() [all[tags]prefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]] [[no-realm]]

\procedure hgsd-realm-selection() [title[$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection]!is[tiddler]limit[1]] :then[subfilter<hgsd-realm-all>] [title[$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection]get[list]enlist-input[]] +[unique[]]

\procedure hgsd-scope-include() [enlist<scope-base>] -[all[tags]prefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]tagging[]] [enlist<scope-tags>tagging[]] :filter[enlist<scope-base>match<currentTiddler>]

\procedure hgsd-scope-exclude() [enlist<scope-tags>tagging[]] :filter[enlist<scope-base>match<currentTiddler>]